repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/UStore
url: https://www.unum.cloud/ustore
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.7537042
    description: "Concept DOI — all versions"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.8263173
    description: "v0.13.12 — version DOI"
abstract: >-
  UStore is a GPU-accelerated embedded transactional database built for high-throughput NVMe
  devices, taking a hyper-converged design where storage and compute share one node rather than
  being disaggregated across a network. Point lookups stay on the CPU, reaching the drive through
  kernel bypass with io_uring passthrough and SPDK and searching tree nodes sized to the medium
  with SIMD kits chosen once when a database opens, while GPUs take over LSM compaction and other
  bulk operations, loading sorted runs straight into device memory through GPUDirect Storage.
  Blobs, documents, and graphs live in multi-modal collections addressed by 128-bit UUID keys,
  with transactions spanning collections, all exposed through one engine-agnostic C ABI and thin
  Python and Rust bindings that forward each call without copying results into language
  containers. A reference in-memory backend on SmashTable ships alongside support for third-party
  key-value stores such as RocksDB and LevelDB behind the same interface.
keywords:
  - database
  - transactional
  - key-value
  - multi-modal
  - nvme
  - io-uring
  - spdk
  - gpu
  - simd

